  nonce: '23e7'  # 23e7
  message: "DECISION + fixed + merged to dev (fast-forward 6b0b6b7464, commit ecbe3cfc01). The two values needed DIFFERENT verdicts: (1) asciidoc/makefile are real taxonomy.LANGUAGES LanguageSpecs that discovery/file-anchors legitimately apply -> CATALOG FIX: all_known_languages() now unions the taxonomy names (the axis catalog = analyzer/linker registration UNION taxonomy = the complete recognized-language set; the two sources genuinely diverge). (2) gradle/csproj are NOT a catalog gap but PRODUCER MISLABELS: manifest_targets._extract_gradle/_extract_csproj stamped the build-manifest FORMAT as Symbol.language, contradicting every sibling extractor (sbt->scala, cabal->haskell, gemspec->ruby, dune->ocaml, nimble->nim). A gradle mainClass is a Java class (.java target_path), a .csproj StartupObject is C# (.cs) -> now emit java/csharp, REMOVING the invalid values rather than registering the leak. Evidence-driven: 9 of 11 manifest extractors already map manifest->target-language; gradle+csproj were the outliers. BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: openzeppelin axis_conformance 36->0, detekt 6->0. Core + mainstream 100% coverage. Also corrected a stale test comment that mis-described the language slot as build-format tokens."  # 23e7
